title RecruitBook System Context Diagram

left to right direction

' ---------- Human actors (cross TB-1: Browser / RecruitBookApp) ----------
actor Student
actor Counselor
actor PlatformAdministrator
actor AdmissionsOfficer

' ---------- Central system boundary ----------
rectangle "RecruitBookApp" as RecruitBookApp <<boundary>>

' ---------- External services ----------
cloud "EmailService" as EmailService <<external>>
cloud "AIService" as AIService <<external>>

' ---------- External data stores ----------
database "Database" as Database <<storage>>
collections "ObjectStorage" as ObjectStorage <<storage>>
collections "SearchIndex" as SearchIndex <<storage>>

' ---------- Actor interactions (TB-1: Browser / RecruitBookApp) ----------
Student --> RecruitBookApp : TB-1: profile creation, consent, AI review
Counselor --> RecruitBookApp : TB-1: verified counselor support
PlatformAdministrator --> RecruitBookApp : TB-1: privileged verification decisions
AdmissionsOfficer --> RecruitBookApp : TB-1: approved admissions discovery

' ---------- External system / data store interactions (trust boundary crossings) ----------
RecruitBookApp --> EmailService : TB-4: verification and invitation emails
RecruitBookApp --> AIService : TB-5: consent-approved narrative fields
AIService --> RecruitBookApp : pending AI contextualization output
RecruitBookApp --> Database : TB-2: protected records with RLS
RecruitBookApp --> ObjectStorage : TB-3: validated transcript files
RecruitBookApp --> SearchIndex : TB-6: published, visible, consent-allowed profiles

' ---------- Security controls enforced inside RecruitBookApp ----------
note bottom of RecruitBookApp
RecruitBookApp enforces:
- AccessPolicy
- RowLevelSecurityPolicy
- AIOutputPolicy
- FileValidationRule
- AuditLogEntry
end note

' ---------- External system / data store security constraints ----------
note right of AIService
AIService cannot publish output directly.
AI output must return as pending and pass
student acceptance, human approval, and AIOutputPolicy.
end note

note right of Database
Database access must be protected by
RowLevelSecurityPolicy and server-side
AccessPolicy checks.
end note

note right of ObjectStorage
Transcript files require FileValidationRule
before protected storage. No public
unauthenticated transcript URLs.
end note

note right of SearchIndex
SearchIndex must not index unpublished, hidden,
consent-restricted, or publication-ineligible profiles.
end note

' ---------- Trust boundary reference ----------
legend right
Trust boundaries
TB-1: Browser / RecruitBookApp
TB-2: RecruitBookApp / Database
TB-3: RecruitBookApp / ObjectStorage
TB-4: RecruitBookApp / EmailService
TB-5: RecruitBookApp / AIService
TB-6: RecruitBookApp / SearchIndex
endlegend

